## Session summary

**Criteria status: NOT yet met** — `dir_reuse_coherency@32/caw` remains the single gap (all other node counts 1/2/4/8/16 and all other 32-node tests PASS). But this session made major diagnostic progress and narrowed the root to a specific, actionable fix.

**What I proved (fully instrumented, RULE 4):**
- The 32-node wedge is **not** a fairness/starvation problem (I spent 4 runs, B2–B5, tuning the CAW yield/streak mechanism — that was the wrong tree). 
- The real root: at the dir-reuse boundary, a peer ends up **holding inode 131's on-disk EX bit while its cached `i_dlm_mode=NL`** — an **orphaned holder bit**. All 31 peers then block 360s → `rc=-110` shutdown cascade. Proven via a new `P-ACQ-STUCK` probe dumping the live slot (e.g. B8: test27 holds `hex=0x4000000`, gen advancing, never releases).
- **Why it forms:** `resource_id` has no inode-generation, so the reused inode maps to the same CAW slot and inherits the prior tenure's bit; the holder's inode reclaim resets `i_dlm_mode→NL` without a CAW release. (Memory-pressure eviction explains why 32 reproduces and 16 doesn't.)
- **Why nothing clears it:** `mxfs_dlm_bast_process`'s orphan-release path (`orphan_live` + strike escalation) is **TCP-only** (`p_rel_gen` is always 0 on CAW), so a CAW incore-NL orphan is never released.

**Fixes built (v0.10.45, in tree):** acquire-side self-`EDEADLK` recovery + holder-side stale-`DEMOTING` re-queue. These pushed the wedge from r2/r3 → **r4** (real progress) but didn't fully clear it.

**Fable consult (RULE 5, justified):** validated the fix design — use a **claim protocol** (CAS state→DEMOTING, re-validate, then clear) to avoid a TOCTOU double-EX; **invalidate not flush** (stale prior-incarnation cache); and the **root fix is reclaim-time release**.

**Formation site located:** `mxfs_dlm_evict` (xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:21934) resets `i_dlm_mode→NL` — the unpublish fast-path (21953) does so with no disk release, and the normal path's `cancel_work_sync` may drop a mid-flight demote. Next session starts here: verify acquire blocks on DEMOTING, instrument evict to confirm the shared dir orphans there, then add the reclaim-time release + minimal BAST-time clear. Full plan is in memory `AAA-ccloopa864-sess2-END-fable-design-and-evict-formation-site`.

